<!-- 01 — FIELDS -->
<section id="fields" class="container" style="padding-block:7rem 1rem;max-width:1100px;">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — Two fields</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;max-width:720px;">Whoever looks interchangeable ends up negotiating on price.</h2>
  <div class="grid-2" style="background:none;gap:clamp(2rem,3vw,3rem);">
    <div class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-num">A</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Industry and technology</h3>
      <p class="card-desc" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">The engineer checks the technology, purchasing checks price and delivery capability, management checks the risk. What is bought is a technology – and the company that will still stand behind it in ten years.</p>
      <p class="card-desc"><a href="/en/case-studies/cobiax/">Cobiax</a> · <a href="/en/case-studies/hella/">Hella</a> · <a href="/en/case-studies/gneuss/">Gneuss</a> · <a href="/en/case-studies/meco/">Meco</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <div class="card-num">B</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Retail and branded goods</h3>
      <p class="card-desc" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">First the buyer decides on the listing, then the consumer decides within seconds at the shelf. Convince only the second, and the product never makes it onto the shelf.</p>
      <p class="card-desc"><a href="/en/case-studies/piasten/">Piasten</a> · <a href="/en/case-studies/albatros/">Albatros</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 — PRINCIPLES -->
<section class="container" style="padding-block:7rem 1rem;max-width:1100px;">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">02 — Principles</p>
  <div class="grid-3" style="background:none;gap:clamp(2.5rem,4vw,4rem);">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div style="width:44px;height:44px;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <img src="/img/icon-home-praezision.svg" alt="" style="width:100%;height:100%;">
      </div>
      <h2 class="display-md" style="margin-bottom:.75rem;">Change only what no longer carries.</h2>
      <p class="card-desc">No change is the rule. A logo, a positioning, a campaign is only touched when a strategic analysis shows it no longer serves its purpose — not because a new idea happens to appeal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <div style="width:44px;height:44px;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <img src="/img/icon-home-uebersetzung.svg" alt="" style="width:100%;height:100%;">
      </div>
      <h2 class="display-md" style="margin-bottom:.75rem;">Technology becomes benefit.</h2>
      <p class="card-desc">The real difference rarely lies in the design. It lies in translating a technical detail into a benefit that means something different to the manufacturer, to retail and to the end customer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2">
      <div style="width:44px;height:44px;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <img src="/img/icon-home-rechtssicherheit.svg" alt="" style="width:100%;height:100%;">
      </div>
      <h2 class="display-md" style="margin-bottom:.75rem;">Legally sound, internationally.</h2>
      <p class="card-desc">A name, a mark, a campaign has to work wherever it is used — in trademark law, in language, in culture. That is checked before an idea falls in love with something that cannot be protected.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 — APPROACH -->
<section class="container" style="padding-block:7rem 1rem;max-width:720px;">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">03 — Approach</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Most of the work has nothing to do with design.</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Design is the smaller part of a mandate. The larger part is getting inside the logic of manufacturers, retail, sales and end customers – and finding, for each stage, the reason that counts there.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A technical detail only becomes a benefit promise once someone understands what it actually means for the end user.</p>
  <a href="/en/agency/" class="btn-arrow reveal reveal-delay-2">The approach →</a>
</section>

<!-- 04 — EVIDENCE -->
<section class="container" style="padding-block:7rem 2.5rem;max-width:720px;">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">04 — Evidence</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Twelve mandates, twelve different starting points.</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The evidence for everything above — company by company, not claimed.</p>
  <a href="/en/case-studies/" class="btn-arrow reveal reveal-delay-2">See case studies →</a>
</section>

